{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"REAL REVIEW-RUN EVIDENCE + one AC I am correcting on the evidence rather than reporting as met.\n\nCommitted artifact: docs/serena-symbol-reference-coaching-sample.md (in this change, so it is repo-verifiable). Five real runs, all 'rebar review-plan --source local --no-sign' against ticket 4b14-8eae-404c-4b16, whose Scope says verbatim 'I went through the tree with grep and these are the files that mention it' and then lists 2 of the 6 files carrying the symbol.\n\nWHAT IS PROVEN LIVE. The criterion fires reliably and correctly: 4/4 agent-tier runs produced a finding at validity 1.0 naming the omitted files, INCLUDING tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py:90 - the monkeypatch.setattr string reference that find_referencing_symbols cannot resolve, i.e. the exact site class that broke epic 061c S1. Contrast case also holds: the same criterion against 061c S1 itself (7468, plan already remediated) fired NOTHING and the review returned PASS.\n\nTWO DEFECTS THE RUNS EXPOSED IN MY OWN SPEC, both fixed:\n1. exec: 1-TURN was wrong. At 1-TURN the criterion ran and emitted nothing even on a deliberately thin plan - a 1-TURN reviewer cannot search code, so it could not name an omitted site, and the rubric rightly forbids speculation. Promoted to exec: AGENT (it now cites real line numbers), and the rubric's 'the plan's own text says it grepped' branch was made independently sufficient.\n2. The move was DEAD BY CONSTRUCTION. The same incomplete-inventory evidence also fires the BUILT-IN G1G2/G6/E4 criteria, which are BLOCKING, while this criterion must stay ADVISORY per AC. Pass-4's coachable union is blocking-first-then-advisory, so a move keyed only on the advisory project id competes last and is never offered - precisely the dead-move failure mode the plan-review gate flagged for the code-review routing. Fixed by widening applies_when to [project.symbol-reference-completeness, G1G2, G6]; it still does NOT fire for empty triggers, project.portability, or security/tests. My own held-out test had encoded the wrong contract ('fires only for this criterion'); corrected under revert-first discipline (narrowed config -> confirmed RED for the right reason -> re-applied -> GREEN).\n\nTHE AC I AM CORRECTING. AC5 asked for 'a REAL run whose output CONTAINS that move'. Across four agent-tier runs the coach never SELECTED it. That is not a misconfiguration and no further config can fix it: the overlay controls APPLICABILITY (deterministically proven in tests - offered for the criterion, G1G2 and G6; 1 of 14 applicable moves in run 5's real trigger set; correctly not offered otherwise), while the coach LLM controls SELECTION and consistently preferred built-in moves. There is no closed enum on move_id, so a project move is structurally pickable - it simply was not picked. So the honest statement of what this story delivers is: detection demonstrated live and reliably; coaching demonstrated as OFFERED deterministically, with its appearance in any single run being a model judgement the overlay cannot guarantee. I am recording that rather than claiming AC5 as written.\n\nAC ALREADY MET AND UNCHANGED: code-review moves were ALREADY overlay-driven (code_review/moves.py::load_move_registry reads .rebar/code_review_moves.json) so no engine wiring was added; the criterion routes to plan_review only, and the ticket records why not code_review; posture is advisory via default_posture with no inert blocking_enabled key; a test proves the criterion id appears nowhere under src/rebar/; and a further test proves all three overlay assets are TRACKED (.rebar/prompts/* is ignored with per-file negations, so the new rubric was initially invisible to git and would have shipped to nobody)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785380394612189001,"uuid":"ef789b22-92cb-454b-b9a5-4304572cd633"}